cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use harnesslab or the agentlab harness in academic work, please cite it as below."
title: "HarnessLab: treating the agent harness as a controlled experimental variable"
abstract: >-
  harnesslab is an open platform for measuring coding agents rather than only scoring them. It pairs a
  small, fully configurable coding-agent harness with a measurement ledger that records every model
  call, tool call, edit, and policy event, and a web platform that varies the harness as an
  experimental factor, reports outcomes with uncertainty, replays trajectories, and intervenes on a
  run while it is still going through a sentinel hook that scores the partial trajectory.
type: software
version: "0.3.0"
date-released: "2026-09-03"
license: MIT
authors:
